.TH tutsort n 0.1 tclutils
.SH tclutils::tutsort
.PP
\fBtsort\fR\-like topological sort in pure Tcl.
.SS API
.CS
::tclutils::tutsort::pairs tokenList
::tclutils::tutsort::text  text
::tclutils::tutsort::file  path
.CE
.PP
Tokens are read in pairs: each pair \fBu v\fR means "u must come before v". A self\-pair \fBu u\fR declares an isolated node with no ordering. Nodes that become free are emitted in first\-seen order (stable). A cycle raises \fBTCLUTILS TUTSORT CYCLE\fR; an odd token count raises \fBTCLUTILS TUTSORT ODD\fR.
.SS CLI
.CS
printf 'a b\nb c\n' | tclsh bin/tutsort.tcl
.CE
